,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-07-03T15:03:06Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T08:30:28Z","closed_at":"2025-07-04T15:24:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108239","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108239","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108239.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108239.patch","merged_at":"2025-07-04T15:24:49Z"},"body":"This fixes the crash (and performance degradation) shown in [this MRP](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107951#issuecomment-3012835784), and arguably fixes the most pressing part about #107951, but does not fix the issue as a whole.\r\n\r\nThis makes it so that Jolt's broad phase gets cleaned up (i.e. quadtree nodes made available) whenever a scene is emptied out completely, like it is when switching scenes in the editor, meaning we get a full \"reset\" on such scene switches, which should prevent us from running out of broad phase nodes and crashing.\r\n\r\nThis also cherrypicks jrouwe/JoltPhysics#1682 in order to fix a bug in `JPH::PhysicsSystem::OptimizeBroadPhase` that would otherwise prevent this from working.\r\n\r\nCC @jrouwe ","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/sta